The potential vulnerability is related to an Insecure File Upload vulnerability. This vulnerability arises because the application accepts user-uploaded images without implementing adequate validation or restrictions on the file types and sizes. If the application does not properly check the content type or the file extension of the uploaded images, it could allow malicious files to be uploaded, which may lead to various attacks such as executing arbitrary code on the server or compromising the integrity of the application. Additionally, without proper handling of the uploaded files, there is a risk of denial-of-service attacks through resource exhaustion or file system manipulation.

